/ActualText (Operations teams run on workflows. When an order webhook arrives, a system may need to check the payload, classify the request, notify the right team, wait for approval, and then take an action.\nIn AI-first products, workflows become more complex because some steps now involve machine judgment. An AI node may read a webhook payload, classify the request, and decide which branch the workflow should take. But this only works if the orchestration engine is reliable underneath.\nThis project involves designing and implementing Relay, an AI workflow orchestration platform that can define workflows as connected typed nodes, trigger runs from webhooks or APIs, execute steps durably in the background, pause for human approvals, validate AI outputs, recover from crashes, and maintain complete run traces.\n)
/K [5]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 390 0 R
/Pg 5 0 R
>>
endobj
