/ActualText (3. Durable Workflow Execution:\(Execute runs asynchronously through a queue and worker. Every step should be persisted so that if the worker crashes, the run can resume from the last completed step instead of starting again.\(\(4. Deterministic and AI Nodes:\(Implement deterministic node types such as http_request, condition, delay, and notify. Also implement an ai node where the model output is validated against a JSON schema before downstream steps can use it.\(\n5. Approval Gates and Sensitive Actions:\(Implement approval nodes where a run pauses until a human approves or rejects it. Sensitive nodes, such as order actions, must not execute unless an approval record exists. This should be enforced by the engine, not by the AI prompt.\(\n6. Traces, Guardrails and Step Cap:\(Store a complete trace for every run, including resolved inputs, outputs, attempts, timing, and token usage for AI steps. Handle prompt-injection payloads safely, prevent duplicate side effects with idempotency keys, and enforce a max-step cap so runaway workflows cannot loop forever.\n)
